B.a3x=new A.cf("What is this app?","The AW139 Power Assurance Calculator helps you verify that your AW139 helicopter engines are producing sufficient power under current environmental conditions, in accordance with the Flight Manual power assurance check procedure.",null)
B.a3f=new A.cf("1 \u2014 Select Configuration","Choose the rotor speed (NR) and inlet filter type that matches your aircraft configuration:\n\u2022 NR 100% or 102%\n\u2022 EAPS (Engine Air Particle Separator)\n\u2022 IBF (Inlet Barrier Filter)\n\u2022 No filter (clean intake)",null)
B.a3y=new A.cf("2 \u2014 Enter Environmental Data","Fill in the current conditions at the time of the check:\n\u2022 Pressure Altitude (ft) \u2014 at the airfield\n\u2022 Torque (%) \u2014 torque set for the check\n\u2022 OAT (\xb0C) \u2014 outside air temperature",null)
B.a3B=new A.cf("3 \u2014 Enter Engine Readings","Record the aircraft registration and the steady-state readings for each engine:\n\u2022 NG (%) \u2014 gas generator speed\n\u2022 ITT (\xb0C) \u2014 inter-turbine temperature",null)
B.a3J=new A.cf("4 \u2014 Read the Results","The calculator displays the limits (Max NG and Max ITT) interpolated from the Flight Manual tables for your conditions.\n\nEach engine reading is compared against the limit:\n\u2022 Green \u25bc \u2014 engine is below the limit (pass)\n\u2022 Red \u25b2 \u2014 engine exceeds the limit (fail)\n\nThe delta value shows the margin to the limit.",null)
B.a3d=new A.cf("5 \u2014 Save & Export","Tap Save to store the check in the history log.\nTap PDF to generate and share a printable report.\nThe history log keeps your last checks for reference.\nSwipe a history entry left to delete it individually.",null)
B.a3v=new A.cf("Graph","Tap the graph preview in the results card to open a full-screen overlay showing your operating point plotted on the Flight Manual performance chart.",null)
